From 4fa83f9c4ce3bdc7a6b13f12b6ec41b1d01e41e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:36:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/51] XEX patches for XEX1-keyed modules; resource-only XEX;
 patched dumps

ApplyPatch derived the patched module's keys with the XEX2 retail/devkit
key only, so delta patches for modules encrypted with the XEX1 key (the
system update's xam.xexp) failed with "patch image key doesn't match". Keep
the key that decrypted the base and use it for the patch.

Accept resource-only XEX images (no PE, e.g. huduiskin.xex) and skip code
hashing for them.

Research: --dump_patched_system_modules="<base dir>|<patch dir>|<out dir>"
applies a system update's patches to the Guide modules (hud, huduiskin, xam,
minimediaplayer, signin) and writes the images before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AFb8CDFE1Ms5NnJH88eG8b
